From: ScorchDroid <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] android: publish non-tank target model info for the port's renderer

TargetDefinition::createTarget works out a target's model, scale,
brightness and rotation, then hands all four to TargetRendererImplTarget
inside `#ifndef S3D_SERVER`. This build compiles that block out, so those
values are computed and immediately discarded and the target keeps no
renderer to ask - which is why trees, buildings and every other landscape
object were simulated (shots collide with them, MovementMap paths around
them) but invisible.

Adds an `#else` beside the existing split that records them for the
port's own renderer, and nothing else. Same shape as the audio (0006),
deform (0010), effect (0011) and tracer (0012) hooks.

diff --git a/src/common/target/TargetDefinition.cpp b/src/common/target/TargetDefinition.cpp
index 22ba22a0..3aa5ef40 100644
--- a/src/common/target/TargetDefinition.cpp
+++ b/src/common/target/TargetDefinition.cpp
@@ -23,6 +23,8 @@
 #include <common/DefinesAssert.hpp>
 #ifndef S3D_SERVER
 	#include <tankgraph/TargetRendererImplTarget.hpp>
+#else
+	#include <TargetModelStore.h>
 #endif
 #include <tanket/Tanket.hpp>
 #include <tanket/TanketShotInfo.hpp>
@@ -275,6 +277,14 @@ Target *TargetDefinition::createTarget(
 				finalModelScale.asFloat(), finalBrightness.asFloat(), 
 				billboard_));
 	}
+#else
+	// Android port: there is no client renderer to hand these to, and the
+	// target keeps none of them, so without this everything needed to draw
+	// a tree or a building is computed here and thrown away. Recorded for
+	// the port's own renderer instead. See TargetModelStore.h.
+	ScorchDroidTargets::push(playerId, modelId_,
+		finalModelScale.asFloat(), finalBrightness.asFloat(),
+		rotation.asFloat(), billboard_);
 #endif // #ifndef S3D_SERVER
 
 	target->getLife().setTargetPosition(position);
